title Copal, instrument-suite roster held at a RED fascia leg
prompt The copal baton and inner prompt, one fruit: roster one unrostered chapter witness, claim it, prove it both ways.
think The inner prompt names one unrostered witness under tools/gen/chapter/. Six were unrostered. I chose instrument_suite_witness.rish, the smallest with a prove-red leg.
think The claim scan read clear. The first witness run timed out at the foreground limit, so it ran in the background into session-output.
think The witness ran RED: limb e113_fascia_health exited non-zero, and its scan reports fascia_health=37 against a floor of 41. That is a measured state of the tree. Lowering the floor would manufacture a green.
think Rostering a RED guard would make the standing roster red for a reason no lap in this seat can repair. I reverted my roster edit and closed the claim, so a peer can take the witness.
obs The claim commit's first two messages were refused by the commit-msg hook for lacking a mechanism word. The third carried the words file and field, and the push went through after a rebase.
obs The rebase conflicted on construction/ITINERARY.md. I took upstream's card and re-carried the nib with the writer. The writer writes the card; it does not amend. The nib now names the claim commit, so this log's follow-up commit carries it forward.
